# D: auto-tune identification: roll then pitch rate-loop multisine (excitation.ID_EXCITE, 0.5-15 Hz, 60 deg/s, 30 s),
# MRAC injection off, default PID gains, fusion 2 (each excite start re-zeroes the flow origin; fusion 3 would pull it
# back mid-run). First excite on this airframe: all values PROPOSED (WP-25), none measured. Then on the ground:
# python -m ground_station.autotune.cli <session> --axis roll   (and --axis pitch). Plan: docs/lab/run-sheet-2026-10-16.md
campaign lab-d-excite
# rate 100 = the ceiling: the firmware telemetry send task runs at 100 Hz (SEND_TASK_HZ, campaign_capture.py:351);
# 6.7x the 15 Hz top line. The live probe may still lower it if the link loses frames. thrust_model adds
# u_gyrox/u_gyroy/u_gyroz (rate PID output = Uc for the frequency response); the core set has gyro PID .FB/.Des + motors.
rate 100
log velocity_loops camera_fusion thrust_model
set g_xy_ctrl_kind=0 g_traj_ff_shift_s=0 g_land_xy_gate_cm=10
takeoff 0.5 mrac_injection=0
hold 8
excite axis=roll signal=multisine f0=0.5 f1=15 amp=60 duration_s=30
hold 3
excite axis=pitch signal=multisine f0=0.5 f1=15 amp=60 duration_s=30
hold 3
land
